;; The interval differential corpus: every KNOWN divergence from a
;; real PostgreSQL, one entry per sample. Generated by
;;   (datahike.fuzz.differential/run-surface :interval 0 0)
;;
;; A divergence NOT listed here fails `bb fuzz interval`. A listed
;; one that now AGREES also fails, with BASELINE DRIFT.
;;
;; WAS 835 of 1043 when this corpus was committed -- an interval
;; was the user's own text and `cast-scalar` had no interval arm.
;; Now 23. What is left is three things, and none of them
;; is the parser:
;;
;;   STORED CARRIER (18) -- a VALUES or derived relation is
;;     materialised into datahike, whose `value-category` has no
;;     interval case, so the carrier is stringified on write and
;;     equality/grouping compare TEXT. Phase 2 step 6, gated on
;;     datahike's extension-defined value types. Expression-position
;;     intervals are correct today.
;;   ARITHMETIC (7) -- the operator functions, still 42883.
;;   VALUE SUBSTITUTION (4) -- `array[<interval>]::text` returns
;;     a cmp-equal but different representative. Order-dependent
;;     (correct as the first query on a fresh server), and the
;;     mechanism is NOT the caches or the templater -- see the
;;     per-entry reason for what is ruled out. A consequence of
;;     the carrier's equivalence being coarser than its text.
;;
;; Baseline 2026-10-05: 23 of 876 samples diverge.
;; By reason: {"ARITHMETIC" 5, "STORED CARRIER" 18}

[{:surface :interval,
  :key "SELECT ('1 day'::interval * 2)::text",
  :reason
  "ARITHMETIC: the operator functions -- the 14 {date,time,timetz,timestamp,timestamptz}_{pl,mi}_interval plus interval_pl/mi/um/mul/div. `date-arith-op` still refuses them with 42883. Month addition is NOT microsecond addition: it goes through j2date/date2j with day clamping, so `'2001-01-31' + '1 mon'` is 2001-02-28."}
